      content:
          '**Vitals**: BP 142/86 mmHg, HR 88 bpm, RR 16, SpO2 94% on RA, Temp 36.8C, BMI 25.0 (was 27.3 three months ago).\n\n**General**: Thin, fatigued-appearing male. Appears older than stated age. Cooperative but low energy.\n\n**Cardiopulmonary**: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs. Lungs with mild diffuse expiratory wheezes. Mild dyspnea with conversation during prolonged sentences.\n\n**Abdominal**: Soft, non-distended. Mild right-sided fullness (known mass). No hepatomegaly. Well-healed midline scar from prior cholecystectomy.\n\n**Musculoskeletal**:\n- **Grip strength**: R 24 kg, L 22 kg (below age-sex norms of ~38-42 kg; meets criteria for low grip strength per sarcopenia definition)\n- **Bilateral knees**: Mild crepitus, ROM 0-120 degrees bilaterally, no effusion. Pain with prolonged standing and stair climbing.\n- **General**: Reduced muscle mass visually apparent in upper extremities and thighs. No edema.\n\n**Functional Assessment**:\n- **30-second chair stand test**: 6 repetitions (below normal of >12 for age/sex — indicates lower extremity weakness)\n- **Timed Up and Go (TUG)**: 14.2 seconds (normal <12 seconds — mildly impaired)\n- **6-Minute Walk Test**: 285 meters (predicted >450 meters for age — significantly reduced cardiopulmonary fitness)\n- **Gait**: Slow, deliberate gait. No assistive device. Mild antalgic component favoring knees.\n\n**Neurologic**: Alert, oriented. Grossly intact. Mild deconditioning-related generalized weakness (4/5 proximally, 4+/5 distally).\n\n**Laboratory (recent)**:\n- Hemoglobin 10.2 g/dL (mild anemia — likely iron deficiency from GI blood loss)\n- Iron 35 mcg/dL (low), ferritin 18 ng/mL (low), TIBC 420 mcg/dL (elevated)\n- Albumin 3.2 g/dL (low), prealbumin 14 mg/dL (low)\n- TSH 6.8 mIU/L (mildly elevated — subclinical hypothyroidism)\n- HbA1c 7.8%, fasting glucose 162 mg/dL\n- Vitamin D 18 ng/mL (deficient)',
